import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 530 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 531 | 2026-10-19 | **Key signatures drill follows the Home lessons; levels say what they cover (her 13:55 and 13:57 notes).** Home is now the base: each concept's drill is rebuilt to match its lessons, one by one; the useful drills the lessons do not cover stay as 'More practice'. Key signatures drill: chips are named for what they cover instead of Level N: Order, Sharp keys, Flat keys, All 15, Relative minor, Last note, then under 'More practice': Signs that change, Coral note, Accidentals, Written right, Listen, Bass staff, My keys. New questions (all 15 key signatures, on the app staff): the Nth sharp or flat; name the major key (sharp keys only, flat keys only, all 15); name the relative minor; 'the piece ends on this note' (the last note drawn on the staff, with its letter) to choose between the major and the minor of that signature. Removed (replaced by the new ones): C, G or F; all five; three sharps or flats. The extras keep their old level numbers so the printed book and old records still line up; the new levels are 11-16 and have no printed worksheet yet. Source `patch533.py`; checked by me, EN and KO, no console errors. Note: the book's page-6 drill description still lists the old 1 to 10; it and the Learn tab inside the drill are for the book rework. The Korean wording of the new labels is mine. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
